{%- comment -%}
  DotAim customizations that have no theme setting to express them.

  Kept in this snippet, rendered from layout/theme.liquid immediately after
  'css-variables', so that stock theme files stay unforked and a Be Yours
  update only ever conflicts on the single render line in theme.liquid.

  Ported from Lush KSA (lush.sa.com), which instead edited snippets/
  css-variables.liquid directly. Deliberately NOT ported: KSA's 'SAR'
  riyal-symbol font and .sar_symbol rule, which are Saudi-only. Qatar is QAR.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- style -%}
  /* Lush brand heading face. Held in the theme's own assets rather than the
     store's Files, so it is versioned in git, travels with the theme, and
     cannot be broken by someone deleting a file in the admin. */
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'LushHandwritten';
    src: url('{{ 'LushHandwritten_Bd.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2'),
         url('{{ 'LushHandwritten_Bd.woff' | asset_url }}') format('woff');
    font-weight: normal;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  :root {
    /* Overrides the theme's Heading font setting. Shopify's font picker only
       offers its own library, so a custom brand face has to be forced here.
       NOTE: this means changing "Heading font" in the theme editor has no
       effect. Recorded in docs/store-settings-ledger.md. */
    --font-heading-family: 'LushHandwritten', var(--font-body-family);
  }

  /* Arabic is cursive: its letters join. The theme applies letter-spacing in
     15 places in base.css (up to 0.3rem) and rtl.css does not reset it, which
     visually severs those joins. Ported from KSA, where it is the one Arabic
     typography fix they carried. */
  html[lang='ar'] * {
    letter-spacing: 0 !important;
  }
{%- endstyle -%}
